WEBVTT

00:00:31.866 --> 00:00:33.492
I won't let you pass.

00:00:33.701 --> 00:00:36.329
Shana, didn't I tell you before?

00:00:36.537 --> 00:00:40.875
That I will never stand with you,
as long as you're a Flame Haze.

00:00:41.083 --> 00:00:45.338
Because the Flame Hazes will never
be able to forgive the Denizens.

00:00:46.339 --> 00:00:50.134
They reject them as something
that is foreign to this world!

00:00:50.343 --> 00:00:54.055
Therefore, I shall create
the paradise Xanadu,

00:00:54.263 --> 00:00:56.515
and take the Denizens from this world.

00:00:56.724 --> 00:01:01.270
And for the first time, they'll live in a
world they want, one that wants them.

00:01:01.479 --> 00:01:03.856
They will truly belong.

00:01:04.065 --> 00:01:09.111
At the same time, this is the one
way to grant Yuji Sakai's wish.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:11.697
Please don't try and stop me.

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:36.722
<i>This is me. My hair streams across...</i>

00:01:36.931 --> 00:01:41.310
<i>...my cheeks dyed red</i>

00:01:41.519 --> 00:01:45.481
<i>I am me... A grain of determination</i>

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:50.236
<i>That was how it began</i>

00:01:50.444 --> 00:02:00.871
<i>If there is a tomorrow that is not
hazed over by hope or despair,</i>

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.248
<i>(simple as that)</i>

00:02:02.456 --> 00:02:04.750
<i>I will not forget</i>

00:02:04.959 --> 00:02:10.298
<i>This pain is the promise we made that day</i>

00:02:10.506 --> 00:02:13.301
<i>I want to make it come true, I can't, I will</i>

00:02:13.509 --> 00:02:20.266
<i>At night I grab the void and awaken
to something in the morning</i>

00:02:20.474 --> 00:02:30.234
<i>I merely soar into the endless sky,
taking the shackles called "reason" Yes,</i>

00:02:30.443 --> 00:02:34.196
<i>"That is all.</i> "

00:02:59.221 --> 00:03:00.639
That's...

00:03:01.682 --> 00:03:05.978
That's the reason you can't be with me?

00:03:08.564 --> 00:03:10.399
Those feelings...

00:03:12.651 --> 00:03:14.779
What we felt back then...

00:03:17.031 --> 00:03:19.742
Why can't you believe them?

00:03:23.412 --> 00:03:24.830
<i>Yum...</i>

00:03:27.708 --> 00:03:30.294
You idiot!

00:03:32.546 --> 00:03:35.257
Idiot!

00:03:38.928 --> 00:03:41.680
Idiot!

00:03:46.769 --> 00:03:48.896
You lived in the world of humans, Master.

00:03:49.105 --> 00:03:52.858
I'm surprised you don't
know how to handle women better.

00:03:53.901 --> 00:03:56.112
That was never a talent of mine.

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:59.740
You could give me several
thousands of years' worth of lessons.

00:03:59.949 --> 00:04:02.993
Unfortunately, it's never
been a talent of mine, either.

00:04:07.331 --> 00:04:08.457
We'll attack that!

00:04:08.666 --> 00:04:10.584
U-Understood, indeed.

00:04:13.921 --> 00:04:16.048
Th-They're...

00:04:17.675 --> 00:04:19.301
Throw me!

00:04:24.932 --> 00:04:27.017
This is the Grand Order Psalm...

00:04:27.226 --> 00:04:30.771
Yes, and this ring is Corde.

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:34.150
A Treasure that can be loaded with an
Unrestricted Method and fired as a bullet.

00:04:34.358 --> 00:04:35.776
I see.

00:04:35.985 --> 00:04:39.238
I don't know how you got the Psalm,

00:04:39.447 --> 00:04:41.407
but I suppose it would be effective.

00:04:41.615 --> 00:04:44.034
I have more than this!

00:04:51.459 --> 00:04:52.877
Take this.

00:05:06.432 --> 00:05:09.560
And I have more than this, as well.

00:05:10.686 --> 00:05:14.648
This is important to me.
I've made it so it can protect itself.

00:05:19.528 --> 00:05:22.490
"What the Wind Calls"

00:05:33.042 --> 00:05:35.044
It doesn't appear to be going well.

00:05:35.252 --> 00:05:38.297
He's pretty strong, too...

00:05:38.506 --> 00:05:39.924
What?

00:05:46.222 --> 00:05:48.974
As usual.

00:05:49.183 --> 00:05:51.310
Yeah, I'm sure it's one of Dad's...

00:05:51.519 --> 00:05:53.938
Sale Habichtsburg!

00:05:54.146 --> 00:06:00.653
Today is our special
"payback for all you've done" day!

00:06:00.861 --> 00:06:02.696
Prepare yourself...

00:06:11.914 --> 00:06:15.751
One-hit kill ultimate weapon!

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:24.885
The miracle of science,
Excellent 252580, the Ultimate Fist Circle!

00:06:31.433 --> 00:06:33.227
I guess this is bad.

00:06:33.435 --> 00:06:35.437
Yeah. Probably.

00:06:43.529 --> 00:06:46.865
Jeez... They're having
all that fun outside.

00:06:47.074 --> 00:06:49.827
Why do I have to stay hidden?

00:06:50.035 --> 00:06:53.372
They're the decoys, and we're
the ones with the real job to do.

00:06:53.581 --> 00:06:56.166
Can't complain about that.

00:06:56.375 --> 00:06:57.876
Yeah, I suppose.

00:06:58.794 --> 00:07:03.841
If we want to help them,
we have to do our job.

00:07:04.049 --> 00:07:06.677
Yeah, I guess, but...

00:07:06.885 --> 00:07:08.762
Will we really make it in time?

00:07:09.263 --> 00:07:14.143
Indeed. I didn't expect
her to be directly above us.

00:07:14.351 --> 00:07:18.772
Yeah, if she's something
they need, they'll protect her well.

00:07:18.981 --> 00:07:20.608
Let's go.

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:48.802
Where did he come from?

00:07:50.929 --> 00:07:52.681
No... More importantly...

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:55.893
He's trying to bring down this tower.

00:08:01.982 --> 00:08:06.028
Bel-Peol! Protect yourself!

00:08:37.976 --> 00:08:40.479
I guess it worked.

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:48.445
Am I going to die?

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:55.828
No... If it ends here, there wasn't
any point in my coming.

00:08:57.496 --> 00:09:00.958
They didn't want to say goodbye,

00:09:01.166 --> 00:09:03.293
but they did anyway.

00:09:04.253 --> 00:09:06.088
There was love.

00:09:06.922 --> 00:09:16.515
<i>As the glow of the sunset
sky dyes the city and your profile</i>

00:09:17.057 --> 00:09:23.188
Sometimes it's still love, even when
you do something they don't want...

00:09:23.188 --> 00:09:29.194
<i>what are you thinking,
watching, and feeling?</i>

00:09:29.194 --> 00:09:30.779
Pheles-san is doing something
Johann-san wouldn't want.

00:09:30.779 --> 00:09:38.746
<i>Even if we can't see our
future further down the road,</i>

00:09:38.746 --> 00:09:39.246
Because they're both in love.

00:09:39.246 --> 00:09:44.918
<i>I will hold your hand</i>

00:09:44.918 --> 00:09:45.210
because she didn't
really want me to use it.

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:52.009
<i>And race to the ends of the earth</i>

00:09:52.009 --> 00:09:52.926
<i>'an.</i>

00:09:53.427 --> 00:09:58.891
<i>All the tears,
lies, sadness, and regrets</i>

00:09:58.891 --> 00:09:59.767
Cut this!

00:09:59.767 --> 00:10:05.564
<i>Are proof that I was here with you</i>

00:10:05.773 --> 00:10:14.281
<i>I believe "goodbye" is the beginning
of memories only couples can have</i>

00:10:14.490 --> 00:10:17.993
<i>So I swear upon my heart</i>

00:10:17.993 --> 00:10:20.120
I'm going to try it.

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:26.543
<i>That someday, again...!</i>

00:10:27.127 --> 00:10:30.422
It will put Sakai-kun in danger.

00:10:30.631 --> 00:10:34.927
It may ruin Shana-chan's plan.

00:10:35.135 --> 00:10:39.223
But I think it's for the best.

00:10:39.431 --> 00:10:41.809
For that, I'm willing
to throw away my life.

00:10:42.017 --> 00:10:43.435
No...

00:10:48.482 --> 00:10:50.484
I won't throw it away.

00:10:52.528 --> 00:10:54.613
I'll make it worth something!

00:11:08.669 --> 00:11:10.838
I heard you.

00:11:11.046 --> 00:11:13.423
So very, very strong...

00:11:21.557 --> 00:11:23.559
Pheles-san?

00:11:23.767 --> 00:11:29.439
The Giralda is a Treasure created to
allow humans to use Unrestricted Methods.

00:11:36.238 --> 00:11:43.370
Humans cannot concentrate
strongly enough on a single thought.

00:11:43.579 --> 00:11:47.082
So it lets them invoke
an Unrestricted Method

00:11:47.291 --> 00:11:51.211
by using their resolve
to sacrifice themselves.

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:53.046
Then I...

00:11:53.255 --> 00:11:54.506
You will not die.

00:11:54.715 --> 00:11:57.634
Did you give me
this because you knew?

00:11:57.843 --> 00:11:58.635
The opposite.

00:11:58.844 --> 00:12:02.931
I gave it to you because I thought
you would never, ever use it.

00:12:04.474 --> 00:12:09.187
But you made this miracle happen,
and brought me here.

00:12:09.396 --> 00:12:11.523
I, who can change everything,

00:12:11.732 --> 00:12:15.068
in the place where
everything is decided...

00:12:22.784 --> 00:12:24.620
Kazumi Yoshida.

00:12:25.245 --> 00:12:30.083
I shall go, in answer to your miracle,
and grant your wish.

00:12:35.505 --> 00:12:36.924
Pheles...

00:12:40.469 --> 00:12:42.846
I shall change what is here,

00:12:43.055 --> 00:12:47.851
and I shall fulfill my
unwanted promise with Johann.

00:12:55.150 --> 00:12:56.401
Pheles...

00:12:56.610 --> 00:12:58.904
Why didn't you tell me anything?

00:13:02.449 --> 00:13:03.825
Pheles!

00:13:04.034 --> 00:13:05.535
I'm sorry.

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:10.082
Pheles!

00:13:14.002 --> 00:13:18.006
To have her summoned here,
at this late hour...

00:13:23.053 --> 00:13:24.471
I have you.

00:13:32.062 --> 00:13:34.064
Wake up, Johann.

00:13:38.819 --> 00:13:40.237
Yo.

00:13:40.487 --> 00:13:42.406
Hello there, I suppose.

00:13:42.614 --> 00:13:45.993
Yuji Sakai-kun and Snake of the Festival.

00:13:46.201 --> 00:13:47.995
I'm taking it back.

00:13:48.203 --> 00:13:53.083
Our Treasure, the Midnight Lost Child.

00:13:53.291 --> 00:13:54.209
Yuji!

00:13:54.418 --> 00:13:56.044
I won't let you!

00:14:01.717 --> 00:14:04.219
If you were inside me,

00:14:04.428 --> 00:14:08.932
then you should know
what Yuji Sakai was planning.

00:14:09.141 --> 00:14:11.059
Both of them, I suppose.

00:14:11.268 --> 00:14:14.438
I can understand
his passion and devotion,

00:14:14.646 --> 00:14:15.981
but I can't agree with it.

00:14:16.189 --> 00:14:16.898
What?

00:14:17.107 --> 00:14:20.527
I don't mind the means,
but I don't like the ends.

00:14:20.736 --> 00:14:21.361
The ends?

00:14:21.570 --> 00:14:26.950
Yes. The ends for
Yuji Sakai-kun, who isn't a God.

00:14:27.826 --> 00:14:32.039
It's a noble vow,
but it's boring and not any fun.

00:14:32.247 --> 00:14:34.583
And more than anything,
everyone ends up unhappy.

00:14:34.791 --> 00:14:36.543
I can't cooperate with that.

00:14:36.752 --> 00:14:38.378
This isn't a game!

00:14:38.587 --> 00:14:43.675
Yuji Sakai-kun, you're trying
to make the ending too clean.

00:14:44.718 --> 00:14:47.345
"I did this, so I have to do that," you say.

00:14:47.554 --> 00:14:49.681
And that forces you into this.

00:14:49.890 --> 00:14:53.310
I'll do everything I can,
and then take the punishment for it.

00:14:53.518 --> 00:14:55.479
What's wrong with that?!

00:14:55.687 --> 00:14:59.107
Isn't it wrong to make
the girl you like unhappy?

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:02.069
If love is behind your whole plan,

00:15:02.277 --> 00:15:05.864
then I think it's okay
to act a bit more selfishly...

00:15:07.157 --> 00:15:09.659
Shana would never allow that.

00:15:09.868 --> 00:15:11.870
You haven't even
told her the whole thing.

00:15:12.079 --> 00:15:13.705
So how do you know?

00:15:13.914 --> 00:15:16.666
You've been so obsessed with
the pursuit of your goal...

00:15:16.875 --> 00:15:20.504
I also think not paying
more attention to her is a mistake.

00:15:21.963 --> 00:15:24.674
You don't think
Shana would understand?

00:15:24.883 --> 00:15:27.552
I'm not optimistic enough to expect that!

00:15:27.761 --> 00:15:31.765
Revealing the plan could
endanger the creation of Xanadu!

00:15:31.973 --> 00:15:33.934
So, your hopes are dangerous...

00:15:34.142 --> 00:15:37.687
You really are stubborn. Or rather...

00:15:37.896 --> 00:15:41.650
I see... I understand now.

00:15:43.819 --> 00:15:47.280
You're underestimating love!

00:15:47.489 --> 00:15:49.282
What?

00:15:49.491 --> 00:15:51.493
You tell yourself you
can't show them your love.

00:15:51.701 --> 00:15:53.829
You won't use it as an excuse.

00:15:54.037 --> 00:15:56.665
You keep making your world smaller.

00:15:58.416 --> 00:16:01.920
Love can push aside logic and self-interest,
and accomplish anything.

00:16:02.129 --> 00:16:04.506
It's pretty amazing.

00:16:04.714 --> 00:16:07.551
You expect me to believe that,
just because you said it?

00:16:07.759 --> 00:16:09.803
I thought you'd say that.

00:16:10.011 --> 00:16:13.515
You've decided that you
can't be allowed to have happiness,

00:16:13.723 --> 00:16:17.644
so you've thrust aside what
you have now, and come this far.

00:16:17.853 --> 00:16:20.272
You have no right to say that to me!

00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:22.691
What I think about it is up to me.

00:16:22.899 --> 00:16:25.026
It's all right, Johann.

00:16:25.235 --> 00:16:26.862
So is doing this.

00:16:33.076 --> 00:16:35.787
It's fine. I'll give it back to you.

00:16:35.996 --> 00:16:37.372
What are you going to do?

00:16:37.581 --> 00:16:41.126
I'm going to change your situation!

00:16:41.334 --> 00:16:43.086
Come here, Pheles.

00:16:43.295 --> 00:16:44.921
Johann!

00:16:48.592 --> 00:16:51.178
I did everything.

00:16:51.386 --> 00:16:53.180
I didn't want to, but I did it anyway.

00:16:53.388 --> 00:16:55.390
I tried really, really hard.

00:16:55.599 --> 00:16:57.267
Thank you, Pheles.

00:16:57.475 --> 00:16:59.436
I'm sorry to make you
do something so painful.

00:16:59.644 --> 00:17:03.190
My beloved Pheles, no one will ever...

00:17:03.398 --> 00:17:04.941
Yes, Johann.

00:17:05.150 --> 00:17:07.986
Tear us apart again...

00:17:27.923 --> 00:17:29.424
Get in!

00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:35.388
Bye!

00:17:37.474 --> 00:17:38.892
Damn!

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:40.268
Floor it!

00:17:40.477 --> 00:17:41.895
Right!

00:17:46.483 --> 00:17:49.152
Go with them for now, Kazumi.

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:52.656
The one that went up was an illusion.

00:17:52.864 --> 00:17:55.575
The real bus was heading toward the surface.

00:17:55.784 --> 00:17:56.409
In other words...

00:17:56.618 --> 00:17:59.204
What a bunch of jerks...

00:17:59.412 --> 00:18:00.830
Yuji!

00:18:01.081 --> 00:18:04.709
You lost your detection ability, didn't you?

00:18:04.918 --> 00:18:06.920
An effect of Johann's leaving?

00:18:07.128 --> 00:18:08.255
I don't know.

00:18:08.463 --> 00:18:12.717
But now I have better things
to do than to find out why.

00:18:33.238 --> 00:18:34.656
What?

00:18:36.741 --> 00:18:39.953
That isn't a nice way to greet a guest.

00:18:40.161 --> 00:18:43.081
Yeah. I'm sorry to
force myself on you like this,

00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:45.417
but do you need an
escort for your escape?

00:18:45.625 --> 00:18:50.505
If they have your strength, sure.

00:18:52.882 --> 00:18:56.011
I didn't expect Hyakki Yakou to show up.

00:18:56.219 --> 00:19:00.015
So the Tuner infiltrated,
to get them inside.

00:19:00.223 --> 00:19:02.892
But what's the point of taking her?

00:19:03.101 --> 00:19:06.646
Who knows? They've caused
a good deal of damage.

00:19:06.855 --> 00:19:10.608
But in the end,
we'll make it all work out.

00:19:12.152 --> 00:19:13.611
Professor.

00:19:13.820 --> 00:19:15.905
Is the tower's tuning not finished yet?

00:19:16.114 --> 00:19:17.824
Yes, General!

00:19:18.033 --> 00:19:22.329
We've just finished the density
calculations and VR simulations...

00:19:22.537 --> 00:19:24.331
Domino!

00:19:24.539 --> 00:19:31.546
Domino, are you trying to
ruin my beautiful climactic scene?

00:19:31.755 --> 00:19:34.758
I'm very sorry, Professor!

00:19:34.966 --> 00:19:36.676
So when will it be done?

00:19:36.885 --> 00:19:38.011
When?

00:19:38.219 --> 00:19:39.679
We can do it whenever...

00:19:39.888 --> 00:19:43.391
We can do it right now, in fact!

00:20:18.551 --> 00:20:23.306
P-Professor! The machinery
control system is exposed!

00:20:23.515 --> 00:20:25.767
Didn't you remove the monster
form control room functions

00:20:25.975 --> 00:20:27.644
when the Strategist got mad at you?

00:20:27.852 --> 00:20:28.937
Domino!

00:20:29.145 --> 00:20:35.235
Call it a self-sacrifice,
to benefit the tower's strength!

00:20:41.199 --> 00:20:43.952
Don't make me worry
about things I haven't planned for,

00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:45.703
Professor Dantalion.

00:20:45.912 --> 00:20:47.747
We're saved...

00:20:47.956 --> 00:20:50.375
Can you send it back inside?

00:20:50.583 --> 00:20:52.585
I'm prepared for anything.

00:20:52.794 --> 00:20:55.088
Close canopy!

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:00.218
Jeez“.

00:21:03.054 --> 00:21:05.723
This wasn't part of the plan,
but we managed to pull it off somehow.

00:21:05.932 --> 00:21:09.727
It might be easier than
just blowing up the whole thing.

00:21:09.936 --> 00:21:12.564
But we'll be destroying
it all, either way.

00:21:12.772 --> 00:21:16.276
Then let's perform the
important task they assigned us.

00:21:16.484 --> 00:21:20.697
Let's do it, and make sure
we don't collapse under the pressure.

00:21:26.536 --> 00:21:29.873
Why do they keep
fighting without advancing?

00:21:30.081 --> 00:21:33.042
We're simply waiting
for Xanadu's creation.

00:21:33.251 --> 00:21:36.671
Time is on our side.

00:21:36.880 --> 00:21:40.258
This is strange.
I don't understand their plan.

00:21:40.258 --> 00:21:43.219
<i>The moon and stars
are illuminating me</i>

00:21:43.428 --> 00:21:46.848
<i>On top of the carpet with
dancing sparks</i>

00:21:47.056 --> 00:21:50.518
<i>You are right in front of me,
glowing red in the light</i>

00:21:50.727 --> 00:21:54.147
<i>Your honest eyes are twinkling</i>

00:21:54.355 --> 00:21:57.734
<i>The two footsteps, they head
toward the distant yonder</i>

00:21:57.942 --> 00:22:02.614
<i>The words I told you said,
"Let's leave everything behind"</i>

00:22:02.822 --> 00:22:08.077
<i>Fly toward the future</i>

00:22:08.286 --> 00:22:12.582
<i>The motive has a strong grasp on
my heart Yes, this is the ultimate descent</i>

00:22:12.790 --> 00:22:16.211
<i>The two of us are fellow soldiers
flattering one another's pulses</i>

00:22:16.419 --> 00:22:19.631
<i>If you are going to protect your love,
you cannot reject battle</i>

00:22:19.839 --> 00:22:23.176
<i>Without fudging a phrase,
we rhyme down this hot path</i>

00:22:23.384 --> 00:22:26.679
<i>Passing each other by, quarreling</i>

00:22:26.888 --> 00:22:30.350
<i>Set free from the enchantment</i>

00:22:30.558 --> 00:22:33.895
<i>If you are going to leave on a journey,</i>

00:22:34.103 --> 00:22:37.649
<i>I will never let go of your hand again</i>

00:22:37.857 --> 00:22:41.152
<i>Do you still remember the first time</i>

00:22:41.361 --> 00:22:44.864
<i>Our eyes locked,
just as it happened?</i>

00:22:45.073 --> 00:22:48.201
<i>Even if I am engulfed
by the vortex of slumber,</i>

00:22:48.409 --> 00:22:54.082
<i>It will not vanish,
I won't let it--It's our dream</i>

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:55.500
<i>To be as ONE</i>

00:22:55.708 --> 00:23:00.338
<i>When you placed your hands
on your cheeks and laughed</i>

00:23:00.547 --> 00:23:02.799
<i>I thought, "I want to protect you"</i>

00:23:03.007 --> 00:23:06.761
<i>We took a roundabout path, huh?
But I've realized</i>

00:23:06.970 --> 00:23:10.390
<i>That I live just for you</i>

00:23:10.598 --> 00:23:13.977
<i>Snow of light flutters down the sky</i>

00:23:14.185 --> 00:23:17.564
<i>Where the waning moon
and stars go to snuggle</i>

00:23:17.772 --> 00:23:21.067
<i>The story we have written</i>

00:23:21.276 --> 00:23:25.405
<i>Will continue on forever</i>

00:23:26.948 --> 00:23:29.534
The battle over the creation
of Xanadu grows fiercer,

00:23:29.742 --> 00:23:32.412
and everyone puts their
lives on the line for their beliefs.

00:23:32.620 --> 00:23:35.331
Meanwhile, Rofocale,
whom Frieder has captured,

00:23:35.540 --> 00:23:37.000
receives an unexpected request.

00:23:37.208 --> 00:23:39.085
Next time,
on Shakugan no Shana Final:

00:23:39.294 --> 00:23:40.795
"The Egg of the World."
